.TH TRAILMATE-LINUX 1 "October 2026" "Trail Mate" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
trailmate-linux \- configurable Trail Mate LVGL desktop application
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B trailmate-linux
.BI --profile " FILE"
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the shared Trail Mate interface in an SDL desktop window.
The selected device profile defines dimensions, rotation, fullscreen policy,
physical keyboard availability and UX pack.
The profile UX pack must match the executable's build composition.
Alt+F4 and window-close requests exit the application and stop its services.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --profile " FILE"
Read the device profile. This option is required.
.TP
.B --windowed
Override the profile's fullscreen setting for this session.
.TP
.BI --quit-after-ms " N"
Exit after N milliseconds in the application loop. Zero disables this limit.
.TP
.BI --screenshot " FILE.bmp"
Save the logical, unrotated UI as a BMP image on exit.
.TP
.B --help
Print usage and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SDL_VIDEODRIVER
Select the SDL desktop backend, for example wayland or x11.
.TP
.B TRAIL_MATE_RUNTIME_MODE
Select local, mesh or demo service behavior. The default is local.
.SH FILES
Device profiles installed by a device package are located under
.IR /usr/share/trailmate/devices/ .
Copy a profile to a user-owned location to customize it and pass that path
with the --profile option.
